.TH CHIMERADB 1 "October 2026" "ChimeraDB" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chimeradb \- initialize and inspect ChimeraDB's MariaDB plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimeradb
.BR setup | status | start
.RI [ "mariadb client options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ChimeraDB exposes MariaDB document collections through the Mongo wire protocol
and through SQL. The command forwards connection arguments to the mariadb client.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Load the catalog and create the mongo() SQL function. Safe to repeat.
Run this after MariaDB has loaded chimera_mongo.
.TP
.B status
Report the server, plugin listener and catalog setup state. Success requires
an active plugin, completed setup and a successful Mongo ping within two seconds.
.TP
.B start
Start the MariaDB service with systemd and report status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo systemctl restart mariadb
sudo chimeradb setup
sudo chimeradb status --socket=/run/mysqld/mysqld.sock --user=root
.fi
.SH MONGO ENDPOINT
For a local SQL UNIX socket, status probes the configured Mongo bind and port
(using 127.0.0.1 for a wildcard bind). All SQL TCP connections require an
explicit CHIMERA_MONGO_HOST: hostnames and aliases may refer to tunnels, so
status does not infer the Mongo endpoint from the SQL host. Set
CHIMERA_MONGO_PORT too when its port differs from the server's configured Mongo
port, as with a forwarded or separate endpoint.
.SH SECURITY
The Mongo listener has no authentication and defaults to 127.0.0.1:27017.
Do not make this endpoint publicly reachable.
.SH UPGRADES AND REMOVAL
The plugin package requires the exact MariaDB version it was built against.
Install a rebuilt plugin together with any MariaDB server update.
ChimeraDB maintainer scripts never connect to the database or run SQL.
MariaDB's own package triggers may restart its service during installation
or upgrade; use a maintenance window.
Removal and purge preserve database data, collections, and catalog tables.
After removal, restart MariaDB to unload the plugin from memory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mysql/mariadb.conf.d/60-chimera.cnf
Listener configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/chimeradb/sql/catalog.sql
Idempotent catalog setup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mariadb (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
